<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="040" project="dotnet-10-upgrade-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-13 — CI setup-dotnet → 10.x / @v6 across all workflows</title>
    <phase>P4 CI/CD + deploy plumbing</phase>
    <gate>032 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies CI workflows (hot path); a wrong pin breaks every gate; ci tag.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Mechanical, enumerated edits across 7 workflow files; bounded.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>CI workflow edits are a shared hot path (ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1 also owns CI); coordinate + keep serial.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>032</deps>
    <tags>ci, dotnet, deployment, migration</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Bump the CI `setup-dotnet` version from `8.x`/`8.0.x` to `10.x`/`10.0.x` and the action from `@v4` to `@v6` across all 7 workflows that reference it (sdap-ci ×5, ci-tier1-blocking ×4, ci-tier2-advisory ×4, deploy-bff-api env, deploy-promote env, nightly-health ×5, adr-audit ×1). Remove any `dotnet-quality: preview` input (post-GA it pulls pre-release patches). Keep `global.json` aligned (global.json overrides the input). Preserve the .NET Framework 4.8 targeting-pack step (net462 plugin build) and apply any allow-list/NoWarn reconciliation from task 032. Ensure CI goes green on net10.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in GitHub Actions, actions/setup-dotnet, and Spaarke's multi-workflow CI topology. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>All 7 workflows resolve a 10.0.x SDK via `actions/setup-dotnet@v6`; no `dotnet-quality: preview` remains; the net462-plugin targeting-pack accommodation stays; the task-032 allow-list/NoWarn reconciliation is applied; CI builds/tests net10 green.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec FR-13 + design §3.3/§7. The 7 workflows + step counts are enumerated in design §3.3. `deploy-bff-api.yml` + `deploy-promote.yml` use an env `DOTNET_VERSION`. The `build-test` job's ".NET Framework 4.8 targeting pack" step (plugin build) MUST stay. The `code-quality` job's plugin-size-gate path is stale (`net48` vs actual `net462`) but guarded by `Test-Path` — note it, do not let this task's scope creep into fixing it unless trivially correct. CI edits overlap `ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1` (CI owner) — `/conflict-check`.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">.github/workflows/sdap-ci.yml</file>
      <file role="modify">.github/workflows/ci-tier1-blocking.yml</file>
      <file role="modify">.github/workflows/ci-tier2-advisory.yml</file>
      <file role="modify">.github/workflows/deploy-bff-api.yml</file>
      <file role="modify">.github/workflows/deploy-promote.yml</file>
      <file role="modify">.github/workflows/nightly-health.yml</file>
      <file role="modify">.github/workflows/adr-audit.yml</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="032" status="pending">CVE allow-list/NoWarn reconciliation available to apply.</dependency>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">global.json already at 10.0.1xx (must stay aligned).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Use `actions/setup-dotnet@v6` with `10.x`/`10.0.x`; REMOVE any `dotnet-quality: preview`; keep global.json aligned (it overrides the input).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">MUST preserve the .NET Framework 4.8 targeting-pack step (net462 plugin build). Do NOT remove plugin-build accommodations.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Run `/conflict-check` before the CI PR — `ci-cd-unit-test-remediation-r1` owns existing CI edits; coordinate.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>CI setup-dotnet bump across the workflow topology</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/cve-audit.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="ci-workflow-topology" location="projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md">design §3.3 — the exact workflow list + step counts.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec FR-13 + design §3.3/§7. Declare RIGOR: FULL. Run `/conflict-check` for CI overlap.</step>
    <step order="1">In each of the 7 workflows, bump every `setup-dotnet@v4` → `@v6` and `8.x`/`8.0.x` → `10.x`/`10.0.x` (incl. the `DOTNET_VERSION` env in deploy-bff-api/deploy-promote).</step>
    <step order="2">Remove any `dotnet-quality: preview` input.</step>
    <step order="3">Confirm the .NET Framework 4.8 targeting-pack step (plugin build) is intact.</step>
    <step order="4">Apply the task-032 allow-list/NoWarn reconciliation in the `code-quality` Dependencies-audit step if needed.</step>
    <step order="5">Push and confirm CI goes green on net10 across the workflows (build-test, eval-gate, code-quality, integration-readiness, compose-fidelity-gate).</step>
    <step order="6">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 040 status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a CI workflow cannot resolve a 10.0.x SDK on the runner (runner image lacks it), STOP and surface — do not pin to a preview channel or downgrade global.json to work around a runner limitation.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Local build parity check</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="config">.github/workflows/*.yml (7 workflows)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">All 7 workflows use `actions/setup-dotnet@v6` with a 10.x/10.0.x version; no `dotnet-quality: preview` remains.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">CI builds/tests net10 green across the workflows (hard gates build-test, eval-gate, compose-fidelity-gate pass).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The .NET Framework 4.8 targeting-pack (plugin build) step is intact.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: global.json remains aligned at 10.0.1xx (no drift between it and setup-dotnet).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-13. Bicep/App-Service runtime strings are task 041; /bff-deploy skill + runbook is task 042.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
